==Trivia==
*The word "Golem" occurs once in the Bible in Psalm 139:16, which uses the word "''golmi''", that means "my light form", "raw" material, connoting the unfinished human being. A golem is an animated, anthropomorphic being in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jewish_folklore Jewish folklore], which is entirely created from inanimate matter, usually clay or mud. The most famous golem narrative involves [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judah_Loew_ben_Bezalel Judah Loew ben Bezalel], the late 16th-century rabbi of Prague.
*The Ice Golem is 1 of 17 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that inspired a troop in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Bats]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Firecracker]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Zappies]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Night Witch]].
**Unlike his [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Ice_Golem counterpart in Clash of Clans], he deals slight damage and merely slows down enemies upon death, rather than freezing them completely and he will slow enemies only after death instead of slowing them even when he attacks them.
**He has a slightly different appearance in Clash Royale, gaining coals, and is smaller-sized in comparison, like a [[Golem|Golemite]].
**He walks with only his legs instead with also both of his hands like the Golem, which is unlike his Clash of Clans counterpart.
*The Ice Golem is 1 of 7 [[cards]] associated with ice, with the others being [[Ice Spirit]], [[Giant Snowball]], [[Freeze]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Super Ice Golem]], and [[Wizard Trio]].
**In the Finnish language setting of the game, the Ice Golem's name translates to "Freezing Golem".
**A Trainer in the [[Training Camp]] is called Trainer Freeze and uses 4 ice-related cards in their [[Battle Decks|deck]], one of them being Ice Golem, and the others being Ice Spirit, Giant Snowball, and Freeze.
*Unlike the Golem, the Ice Golem attacks with both hands, whereas the Golem only punches with one hand. The [[Elixir Golem]] attacks with both hands, but the Elixir Golemites use one hand and the Elixir Blobs appear to bite.
*The Ice Golem, along with the [[Minions]], Bomber, [[Skeletons]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], Ice Spirit, [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Dart Goblin]], Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Guards]], Baby Dragon, [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], Giant Skeleton, Golem, [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Executioner]], [[Mega Knight]], Inferno Dragon, Royal Ghost, and [[Lava Hound]], are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*Unlike the Golem and Elixir Golem, the Ice Golem doesn't spawn his smaller versions upon death.
*The Ice Golem is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Ice Golem is the subject of 3 [[Emotes]].
**The Ice Golem is the subject of a [[King's Tower|Tower Skin]].
*The initial balance change for Ice Golem on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/7/2025)|8/7/2025 balance changes]] was a 12% hitpoints increase, but it was lowered to 10% [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-73-balance-wip-july-2025 last minute].

